Orbit developer onboarding, multi-repo sync, and dev stack orchestrator. (Shortcut: 'o')

Usage:
  orbit [flags]
  orbit [command]

Available Commands:
  admin       Manage platform ownership verification and root cryptographic secrets
  assets      Sync gitignored media with private Cloudflare R2
  audit       Audit workspace versions, dependencies, agents and delivery
  ci          Point private repositories at the self-hosted pool and sync secrets
  completion  Generate zsh autocompletion
  config      Manage Orbit CLI configuration
  dev         Control and orchestrate local development stacks and containers
  doc         Generate documentation and man pages for Orbit CLI
  doctor      Run pre-flight system diagnostics and environment health checks
  env         Manage and validate workspace environment variables and .env files
  help        Help about any command
  init        Clone and initialize workspace repositories
  invite      Manage developer onboarding invite tokens
  migrate     Run and inspect workspace state migrations
  onboard     Interactive onboarding wizard with resume, claims, and stack provisioning
  port        Manage and inspect the hybrid 50-port allocation model
  pr          Manage pull requests and automated delivery
  release     Inspect and promote release pull requests and demo branches
  repair      Attach .git to gitless workspace trees without overwriting files
  self-update Update the Orbit CLI binary to the latest release
  staff       Manage Orbit staff via the staff control plane
  status      Show git status and working tree cleanliness across workspace repositories
  sync        Fetch and fast-forward clean default branches across workspace repositories
  uninstall   Uninstall Orbit CLI binaries and cleanup shell configuration
  update      Unified workspace update (CLI, git branches, migrations, and env validation)
  version     Print the CLI version and build metadata

Flags:
      --config string   Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file
  -h, --help            help for orbit

Use "orbit [command] --help" for more information about a command.
